Subject: [PATCH] watchdog: dw_wdt: allow AR9311 stock recovery to start after restart

The P1 stock boot path fails to re-enumerate with the minimum TOP restart
timeout; normal watchdog expiry with a longer timeout reaches recovery.
The vendor restart handler programs TOP=8 for clocks up to 25 MHz. Select a
TOP of at least one second for the AR9311 integration, using its actual clock
and timeout table. Other Synopsys integrations retain their current behavior.

--- a/drivers/watchdog/dw_wdt.c
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/dw_wdt.c
@@ -302,7 +302,15 @@
 {
 	struct dw_wdt *dw_wdt = to_dw_wdt(wdd);
 
-	writel(0, dw_wdt->regs + WDOG_TIMEOUT_RANGE_REG_OFFSET);
+	u32 top = 0;
+
+	/* AR9311's boot path needs time to service the still-running watchdog.
+	 * TOP=0 resets again before P1 stock recovery can bring USB back. The
+	 * vendor driver uses TOP=8 at 24 MHz; allow at least one second here.
+	 */
+	if (of_device_is_compatible(wdd->parent->of_node, "artosyn,ar9311-wdt"))
+		dw_wdt_find_best_top(dw_wdt, 1, &top);
+	writel(top, dw_wdt->regs + WDOG_TIMEOUT_RANGE_REG_OFFSET);
 	dw_wdt_update_mode(dw_wdt, DW_WDT_RMOD_RESET);
 	if (dw_wdt_is_enabled(dw_wdt))
 		writel(WDOG_COUNTER_RESTART_KICK_VALUE,
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/watchdog/snps,dw-wdt.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/watchdog/snps,dw-wdt.yaml
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@
       - const: snps,dw-wdt
       - items:
           - enum:
+              - artosyn,ar9311-wdt
               - rockchip,px30-wdt
               - rockchip,rk3066-wdt
               - rockchip,rk3128-wdt
